[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue: the parser reads dates month first. The reports say
three. They were merged by subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)),
and the subject does not tell one problem from another. Each problem now has a ticket of its own.

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued parser fix closes only the first problem. The other two stay open after it ships.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {issues} />

### `parser`: the shared parser reads every date month first

A day-first tenant writes 7 April as 07/04. The parser reads it as 4 July, and the invite and the
reminder go out on that day. It happens on every channel and for every tenant on file. This is
the fix that is queued for #4471.

### `hint`: the booking-v3 form tells day-first tenants to type the month first

booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. The tenant's people type what the hint
says, and the form reads the date the tenant's way, day first. The date flips before the parser
sees it. It happens only through the form of the tenants that run booking-v3. The parser fix
does not change it: the hint and the reading of the form must agree.

### `one-day`: dates move by one day, not by a flip

These reports do not show a month and a day swapped. A Tuesday shows as a Monday, every booking
in June is one day off, and one meeting came out on two different days for two clients in two
cities. One invite arrived before the booking was made. That points to time zones or summer
time, not to the order of day and month. The desk noted these reports as a one-day move
(`desk-notes.json`) but counted them under `parser`.

## What the old table shows

The table on #4471 files every report by its tenant, so the one-day reports count as `parser`.
It is here so the two tables can be compared.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## How to read a report

- Read the body. The subject line and the intake tag are not the cause. Intake guesses the tag from the
  reporter's browser, and the browser is often not the tenant's locale.
- The export repeats some reports on overlapping pages. Count each report id once.
- When the cause is not clear, keep the report on its own ticket and say why.

